Saved successfully — no license error, no upsell, identical outcome to the gallery-app case.

Provisioning: Get started > New provisioning configuration. Admin credentials form appeared
directly (auth method "Bearer authentication", Tenant URL + Secret token fields) — same as the
gallery app's form shape but generic rather than Salesforce-specific, since there's no pre-built
connector for a custom app. No upsell or license message. Entered junk values (Tenant URL
"https://a3test.district.local/scim", a fake secret token) and clicked "Test connection."

Result:
  Error code: CredentialValidationUnavailable
  Error details: "We received this unexpected response from your application: Message: An error
  occurred while sending the request. Please check the service and try again."
This is a network/protocol-level failure — Entra actually attempted to reach the fake SCIM
endpoint and got no valid response, since a3test.district.local doesn't exist. Not a licensing
refusal; same shape of wall as the gallery-app case (no real backend to test against), not a
different one.

