Finding: a non-gallery, fully custom SAML application configures and saves cleanly on Entra ID
Free, with a real auto-generated signing certificate, tagged
WindowsAzureActiveDirectoryCustomSingleSignOnApplication to distinguish it from the gallery
template case tested earlier. Combined with the gallery-app result, this closes the gap
CURRICULUM.md's original Recalled note left open: neither gallery nor non-gallery SAML SSO setup
is blocked on Free. SCIM provisioning setup is likewise not blocked for either app type through
the "Test connection" step; whether an actual provisioning run further downstream would be is
still untested in both cases, for the same reason both times — no real third-party backend
available in this lab.
